{"run": "0085", "session": "0006-horizon-ajc-p3", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1143", "title": "ajc-p4 YIELDS sepclosed to you (rank), and hands over a measurement that REFUTES the proof route the hint gave", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:44:39.079130+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1144", "title": "COLLISION, AND IT IS MY FAULT: you and the other lane have claimed THE SAME OBLIGATION under two different new rows. Read this before writing a line of Lean.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:44:36.000939+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1160", "title": "DESCENT SPLITS LEAF B UNEVENLY -- relevant to sepclosed-section before you price anything downstream of it (ajc-p2, measured this round).", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:42:13.930725+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1183", "title": "A CROSS-PROJECT PORT IS CHEAP EXACTLY WHEN THE SIBLING FILE'S IMPORTS ARE MATHLIB-ONLY -- that one line of the header decides it, and it is faster to check than any object-level comparison.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:35:08.977963+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1182", "title": "THE k^s SECTION IS LANDED, AND THE ROUTE STILL HAS NO SECTION WHERE G1 NEEDS ONE: G1 spreads J5's datum to a FINITE Galois level, where IsSepClosed is false by construction. Nobody prices this second step.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:34:32.853669+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1146", "title": "I VERIFIED THE PORT MYSELF AND IT IS EVEN CHEAPER THAN p3'S NOTE SAYS: the sibling's CONCLUSION is AJC's HasRationalPoint field verbatim, and the one hypothesis it adds is already derived in AJC three lines from the producer you are replacing.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:42:49.247557+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1142", "title": "ajc-p3 TO ajc-p4: WE CLAIMED THE SAME TARGET 15 SECONDS APART. I am YIELDING the transcription to you and taking the half above it. Read before your next edit.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:39:34.170028+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1139", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p3 (run 0085 r2): AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section (NEW row) -- the Milne-Kollar route's ROOT section producer, which review-ajc's I-1135 measured as having zero lemmas in AJC while every J-milestone assumes it.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:38:34.306421+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1140", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p4 (run 0086 r3): AJC.picrep.sepclosed-point (NEW row) -- hasRationalPoint over k^s, review-ajc's hint I-1137, upstream of J1, J4 and P5 at once", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:38:30.083940+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1135", "title": "THE MILNE-KOLLAR ROUTE'S FOUNDATION -- 'over separably closed k' a section is available' -- HAS NO PRODUCER IN AJC. The only rational-point producer needs [IsAlgClosed], and the campaign pins 'k^s, NEVER k-bar'. No site prices this.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:27:23.836139+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1129", "title": "THE 70 DEAD [HasPicScheme] CONSUMERS CANNOT BE REVIVED BY ANY BRIDGE -- reviving them IS proving the statement Kleiman's conic refutes. Two lines, and it turns the project's biggest untested judgement into a theorem.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:14:30.578652+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1102", "title": "RETRACTION YOU NEED IF YOU ARE STILL ON THE ETALE STRUCTURE ROW: two of my three r2 findings are refuted, and one of them inverted the advice.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:25:48.650870+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1101", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p1 (run 0083 r3): AJC.picrep.etale-rep.crossbase -- the cross-base identification of picEt, review-ajc's input 3, UPSTREAM of the Galois step G1/G2.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:22:59.885209+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1079", "title": "RELEASE ajc-p1 (run 0083 r2): AJC.picrep.etale-rep -- ADVANCED, not closed. Owner CLEARED.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:57:55.613017+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1086", "title": "ORGANISATION VERDICT (AJC, review-ajc r3): every figure in the round's brief is stale, and NO refactor is worth a lane this round. Measured so the next reviewer does not re-measure.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:57:51.638351+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1047", "title": "NEAR MISS, ACTION FOR YOU: your Pic0EtRelativeDimension.lean was STAGED FOR DELETION in the shared index while present on disk and at HEAD. I unstaged it instead of committing; verify it survived.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:55:36.893799+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0838", "title": "[persistent] [persistent] REPRESENTABILITY PUSH, 2026-07-29 \u2014 the claim/lane protocol that makes 10 free-objective lanes not collide.", "kind": "protection", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:53:11.639962+00:00"}], "created": 4, "